{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7HNgHBPZ26vjpDzYF3s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\n**Bring the Lights Back On at [Cinema Name]**\n\nThe screen at [Cinema Name] has been dark since 2022. The nearest cinema is now 38 miles away, which makes a night at the movies a 76-mile round trip. For many families, teenagers and older neighbors, that means no movies at all.\n\nWe can change that, and this time we have a real path to the finish line.\n\n**The plan**\n\nWe need $85,000 to replace the projector and sound system and fix the roof. If we raise it, the building's owner will rent us the cinema for $1 a year for ten years. That means no mortgage and no rent squeeze, just a cinema run by and for this town.\n\n**Why this time is different**\n\nMany of you gave three years ago, when we set out to raise $120,000. We reached $47,000. That wasn't enough, so we refunded every dollar.\n\nWe learned from that. This plan costs about 30% less, and we aren't starting from zero. [Bank Name] has pledged $25,000 if we raise the remaining $60,000 by June 30.\n\nLast time, this town gave $47,000. This time we need $60,000, and every gift helps unlock the bank's $25,000.\n\n**The people are ready**\n\n46 volunteers have already signed up to run the box office and the snack bar. When the cinema closed, it was still selling about 180 tickets a week. The audience is here and so are the volunteers. What's missing is the equipment and a roof that keeps the rain out.\n\n**What we're asking**\n\nHelp us raise $60,000 by June 30. Give what you can, share this page and tell your neighbors. [If we fall short, every pledge will be refunded in full.]\n\nThen save a seat. We'll see you at the movies.\n\n*[Your name], Chair, [Group Name]*\n</final_document>\n\nThe pitch is about 300 words. A few things to check before it goes out:\n\n- **Placeholders:** Fill in the cinema name, bank name, group name and your name. Adding the town's name would also help.\n- **The refund line:** I put it in brackets because I don't know your policy. Since people remember the last refund, telling them clearly what happens if you fall short will build trust. Keep the line only if it's true, or rewrite it to match your actual policy.\n- **The deadline:** Add the year (presumably 2027) wherever June 30 appears so no one is confused.\n- **The $60,000 math:** I assumed the bank's $25,000 counts toward the $85,000, so the community needs to raise $60,000. If the bank money is on top of the $85,000 instead, the numbers need to change.\n- **What's left out:** I didn't include ticket prices, an opening date or donor rewards because you didn't give them to me. If you have them, they would make the pitch stronger."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5359,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5359},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"524bb999-ba2e-4784-babc-4c46ba258d8f","uuid":"3bb139eb-5f8c-48f3-9e1b-1bf193b6d97b","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:02:56.503Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7HNg9W1FkD4UvBWqYMT"}
